  "year": 2021,
  "arxivId": "",
  "abstract": "Large language models can memorize and leak individual training examples, including sensitive information like names, phone numbers, and email addresses. This paper demonstrates a simple and efficient method for extracting verbatim sequences from a language model's training set using only black-box query access. The attack is possible even though each of the above sequences is included in just one document in the training data.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Large language models <strong>memorize and leak individual training examples</strong>, including sensitive information. This is possible because certain worst-case training examples are <strong>memorized by the model</strong>, even if they don't have noticeably lower losses than test examples on average.",
