    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The attack works by <strong>generating a large, diverse set of high-likelihood samples</strong> from the model, and then <strong>sorting each sample using one of six different metrics</strong> that estimate the likelihood of each sample using a separate reference model. The samples with an abnormally high likelihood ratio between the two models are then extracted as potentially memorized training examples.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
        "description": "A flow diagram showing the steps involved in the attack, including generating samples, sorting them using different metrics, and extracting potentially memorized examples.",
